---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { pipeline } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
  title="Architecture — Inti Cerda"
  description="How a 16-service, event-driven media intelligence platform fits together: ingestion pipeline, Redis Streams event bus and gateway authentication."
>
  <section class="pagehead">
    <p class="pagehead__eyebrow">Architecture</p>
    <h1>Sixteen services, one event bus, no shared database.</h1>
    <p class="pagehead__body">
      Every service owns its own PostgreSQL database and talks to the rest only
      through Redis Streams. These diagrams describe the system that is running
      in production today.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="section__label">01 — Ingestion path</p>
    <ol class="flow reveal">
      {
        pipeline.map((stage, i) => (
          <li class="flow__stage" style={`--i:${i}`}>
            <span class="flow__step">{stage.step}</span>
            <span class="flow__name">{stage.name}</span>
            <span class="flow__detail">{stage.detail}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
    <p class="pagehead__body">
      A scrape run fans out across 160+ outlets with Playwright, dedups against
      Redis, then hands each article to a local model for domain
      classification. Embeddings land in pgvector so the whole corpus stays
      semantically searchable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="section__label">02 — Event bus topology</p>
    <figure class="figure reveal">
      <div class="figure__body">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 820 400" role="img" aria-labelledby="busTitle">
          <title id="busTitle">
            Producers publish to Redis Streams; consumers subscribe. No service
            calls another service's database.
          </title>

          <!-- Producers -->
          <rect class="dg-box" x="60" y="40" width="200" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="76" y="66">web-scraper-core</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="76" y="83">Playwright + LLM classify</text>

          <rect class="dg-box" x="330" y="40" width="180" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="346" y="66">media-billing</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="346" y="83">Stripe webhooks</text>

          <rect class="dg-box" x="580" y="40" width="180" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="596" y="66">media-alerts</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="596" y="83">rule engine</text>

          <!-- Producer drops -->
          <path class="dg-line" d="M160 96 L160 190"></path>
          <path class="dg-line" d="M420 96 L420 190"></path>
          <path class="dg-line" d="M670 96 L670 190"></path>

          <!-- The bus -->
          <path class="dg-line" d="M40 190 L780 190" stroke-width="4"></path>
          <text class="dg-note" x="40" y="178">REDIS STREAMS</text>

          <text class="dg-sub" x="170" y="182">article.classified</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="430" y="182">tenant.plan.changed</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="560" y="182">alert.triggered</text>

          <!-- Travelling packets -->
          <rect class="dg-packet" x="0" y="185" width="10" height="10"></rect>
          <rect
            class="dg-packet"
            x="0"
            y="185"
            width="10"
            height="10"
            style="--d:1.1s"></rect>
          <rect
            class="dg-packet"
            x="0"
            y="185"
            width="10"
            height="10"
            style="--d:2.2s"></rect>

          <!-- Consumer risers -->
          <path class="dg-line" d="M120 190 L120 290"></path>
          <path class="dg-line" d="M330 190 L330 290"></path>
          <path class="dg-line" d="M540 190 L540 290"></path>
          <path class="dg-line" d="M700 190 L700 290"></path>

          <!-- Consumers -->
          <rect class="dg-box" x="40" y="290" width="170" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="54" y="316">media-alerts</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="54" y="333">evaluates rules</text>

          <rect class="dg-box" x="245" y="290" width="200" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="259" y="316">compliance-intel</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="259" y="333">LLM enrichment</text>

          <rect class="dg-box" x="470" y="290" width="150" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="484" y="316">media-auth</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="484" y="333">plan &amp; limits</text>

          <rect class="dg-box" x="645" y="290" width="135" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="659" y="316">notifications</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="659" y="333">telegram · mail</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="figure__caption">
        Producers never call consumers. Adding a consumer means subscribing to a
        stream, not editing an upstream service.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="section__label">03 — Request authentication</p>
    <figure class="figure reveal">
      <div class="figure__body">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 820 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="authTitle">
          <title id="authTitle">
            Traefik verifies every request with forwardAuth, then checks the JWT
            signature against a cached JWKS instead of calling the identity
            provider each time.
          </title>

          <rect class="dg-box" x="20" y="90" width="130" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="34" y="116">Client</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="34" y="133">JWT bearer</text>

          <path class="dg-line" d="M150 118 L235 118"></path>
          <path class="dg-line" d="M225 112 L235 118 L225 124"></path>

          <rect class="dg-box" x="235" y="90" width="175" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="249" y="116">media-gateway</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="249" y="133">Traefik v3 · forwardAuth</text>

          <!-- JWKS side trip -->
          <path class="dg-line" d="M322 90 L322 40 L520 40"></path>
          <path class="dg-line" d="M510 34 L520 40 L510 46"></path>
          <rect class="dg-box" x="520" y="12" width="160" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="534" y="38">media-auth</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="534" y="55">RS256 · JWKS</text>
          <text class="dg-note" x="332" y="32">public keys, cached</text>

          <path class="dg-line" d="M410 118 L495 118"></path>
          <path class="dg-line" d="M485 112 L495 118 L485 124"></path>

          <rect class="dg-box" x="495" y="90" width="185" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dg-label" x="509" y="116">downstream service</text>
          <text class="dg-sub" x="509" y="133">org_id · plan · rate_limit</text>

          <rect class="dg-packet" x="0" y="113" width="9" height="9"></rect>
          <rect
            class="dg-packet"
            x="0"
            y="113"
            width="9"
            height="9"
            style="--d:1.6s"></rect>

          <text class="dg-note" x="20" y="200">
            Claims travel in the token, so no service needs a lookup to know the
            caller's plan.
          </text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="figure__caption">
        The gateway is the only component exposed to the internet. Everything
        behind it trusts the forwarded claims.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="section__label">04 — Screens</p>
    <div class="panel reveal">
      <h2>What this looks like from the front.</h2>
      <p class="pagehead__body">
        The marketing site, the product and the internal operations panel that
        watches this pipeline run.
      </p>
      <div class="actions" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <a class="btn btn--solid" href="/screens/">See the screens</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.875em;
    border: var(--border) solid var(--rule);
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
  }
</style>
